        "theme":  "Enterprise",
        "summary":  "A rigorous framework for measuring generative AI return on investment once deployments move from pilot to production defines ROI as net workflow value over a period with full life-cycle costs accounted for. The framework covers baseline establishment, detailed cost equations, a metrics stack that connects AI activity to business outcomes, and cohort-based rollout instrumentation. The article warns against optimistic time-savings estimates and argues sustainable value requires careful use-case selection and disciplined cost management.",
        "execSummary":  "This is one of the most operationally useful AI strategy articles published this week—it gives enterprise leaders a concrete methodology for justifying and governing production AI spend, not just pilot approvals. The emphasis on full life-cycle cost accounting (including inference, maintenance, and human review costs) directly challenges the ROI narratives most vendors present during sales cycles. For customer-support leaders, the cohort-based rollout model provides a defensible way to measure agent impact on resolution rates, handle time, and cost-per-contact before committing to full deployment. The framework requires instrumentation investment upfront, which must be budgeted alongside the AI deployment itself.",
        "vendorLean":  "Neutral",
