        "title":  "Microsoft releases .NET SDK for AG-UI agent-user interaction protocol",
        "source":  "InfoWorld",
        "url":  "https://www.infoworld.com/article/4227233/microsoft-releases-net-sdk-for-ag-ui-agent-user-interaction-protocol.html",
        "date":  "2026-09-27",
        "theme":  "Platforms",
        "summary":  "Microsoft has released a .NET SDK for AG-UI (Agent-User Interaction), a standardized event-based protocol for agent-to-application communication developed with CopilotKit. The SDK is available on NuGet under MIT license and includes five packages covering protocol events, formatting, protobuf codec, HTTP client integration, and server-side adapters. AG-UI manages eight event categories including lifecycle, messaging, tool calls, and state synchronization, enabling C# developers to build interoperable agent interfaces.",
        "execSummary":  "AG-UI\u0027s .NET SDK release is a meaningful infrastructure signal: Microsoft is investing in open, standardized protocols for how agents talk to applications—which, if widely adopted, could reduce the fragmentation that currently makes multi-agent enterprise systems brittle. For enterprise architects, the MIT license and NuGet availability lower adoption friction, but the protocol\u0027s long-term value depends on whether AG-UI achieves critical mass alongside MCP and other emerging standards. .NET-heavy organizations (a large share of enterprise Microsoft shops) should evaluate AG-UI as a candidate standard for their agent integration layer rather than building proprietary connectors. Protocol fragmentation is real—betting on AG-UI requires monitoring the broader standards landscape over the next 12-18 months.",
        "vendorLean":  "Leans Microsoft — covers Microsoft\u0027s own SDK release for a protocol co-developed with a Microsoft-adjacent partner.",
        "imageUrl":  "https://www.infoworld.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/4227233-0-74496400-1790524589-shutterstock_1536940715.jpg?quality=50\u0026strip=all\u0026w=1024",
        "isNew":  true
