        "summary":  "Google has launched the Gemini desktop app for Windows, enabling users to access AI assistance via the Alt + Space keyboard shortcut without interrupting their workflow. The application supports document and presentation help, task management through Gemini Spark, and creative content generation with image and video tools. Available globally for Windows 10 and 11, the lightweight app is designed to operate in the background without impacting system performance.",
        "execSummary":  "Gemini\u0027s Windows desktop app is a direct competitive move against Microsoft Copilot on its home turf, offering enterprise workers an always-available AI assistant natively on Windows without requiring a browser. The Alt+Space shortcut model mirrors productivity patterns already established by tools like Spotlight and PowerToys, reducing friction to AI adoption for non-technical enterprise users. For customer-support and enterprise-operations leaders, this raises a practical governance question: with multiple AI assistants now installable on the same Windows endpoint, organizations need AI tool policies that address data egress, context leakage, and acceptable-use boundaries. The lightweight footprint reduces the IT objection barrier, which could accelerate shadow-AI adoption if governance is not proactive.",
